# LF in the working tree on every system for the files whose bytes are a contract
# (worfy-windows ticket 02). Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and would check them
# out with CRLF: a script read by bash or zsh on another system would see `\r`, and the hashes of
# build/brand/*.svg in build/icons.json would not match. The index is LF already.
# Other text files keep the checkout settings of each machine.

# Scripts: shell and Node scripts, everything under scripts/.
# harness/ whole: the Harness CLI (no extension), hooks.json and the rules that inject-rules hands to a
# session as they are, and the agents, skills, profiles/README.md and .mcp.json that the Harness shell
# tests read with grep — a `\r` at the end of a line breaks the match (worfy-windows ticket 71).
harness/** text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
scripts/** text=auto eol=lf

# The brand sources of the app icon: build/icons.json records their sha256.
build/brand/*.svg text eol=lf

# The Flight Recorder fixtures are byte for byte as recorded: a later ticket reads the transcripts from a byte
# offset, which CRLF on a Windows checkout would move.
test/fixtures/flight-recorder/** -text
